<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Flavor manifest, WeaselPlex only. Upstream flavors are untouched.

  Points android:banner at a PLAIN PNG instead of @mipmap/ic_banner, which resolves
  to the anydpi-v26 bitmap XML wrapper.

  Why: the launcher tile rendered at roughly half the size of comparable apps.
  Measured on the SHIELD row, both from 640x360 banners with ~85% content fill:
  WeaselCheck 534px wide, this tile 296px. The manifests differ in exactly one way.

    WeaselCheck  banner=res/drawable-mdpi-v4/signal_check_banner.png   plain PNG
    WeaselPlex   banner=res/wH.xml                                     bitmap XML

  Changing the wrapper gravity from fill_horizontal|center_vertical to fill was
  tried first and moved the rendered width not at all, still exactly 296px, so the
  wrapper itself rather than its gravity is what the launcher measures differently.

  ic_banner_art has no anydpi variant, only real PNGs at mdpi, hdpi, xhdpi, xxhdpi
  and xxxhdpi, so this resolves to a BitmapDrawable with honest intrinsic bounds.

  The anydpi wrapper stays in place for @mipmap/ic_banner. Deleting it would fall
  through to the main source set adaptive-icon, whose opaque background renders the
  tile as a solid block on the launcher row.
-->
<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools">

    <application
        android:banner="@mipmap/ic_banner_art"
        tools:replace="android:banner" />

</manifest>
